{"id":100,"date":"2016-05-16T12:48:34","date_gmt":"2016-05-16T12:48:34","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/masterbadminton.dev\/how-to-hit-the-badminton-underarm-clear-forehand-and-backhand\/"},"modified":"2023-08-16T06:10:01","modified_gmt":"2023-08-16T06:10:01","slug":"badminton-underarm-clear-html-html","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/badminton-underarm-clear.html","title":{"rendered":"How to Hit the Badminton Underarm Clear (Forehand and Backhand)"},"content":{"rendered":"<div id=\"ContentColumn\">\n<div class=\"Liner\">\n<div style=\"float: left; margin-right: 10px;\"><\/div>\n<table border=\"1\" width=\"400px\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" align=\"center\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td bgcolor=\"#eb7d2e\" width=\"50%\" height=\"20px\"><span style=\"color: #fbfbef; font-family: Arial; font-size: small;\"><strong>Badminton Underarm Clear<\/strong><\/span><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td bgcolor=\"#ffffff\" width=\"50%\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Arial; font-size: small;\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Arial; font-size: small;\"><br \/>\n<\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<table border=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Level<\/strong><\/td>\n<td>Beginner<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Type<\/strong><\/td>\n<td>Defensive<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Pre-requisite<\/strong><\/td>\n<td>None<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p><span id=\"forehand\" style=\"font-size: 18.6px; color: #ff3300;\"><b>Forehand and Backhand Badminton Underarm Clear<\/b><\/span><\/p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter wp-image-3277 \" src=\"http:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/05\/Underarm-v3.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"658\" height=\"468\" srcset=\"https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/05\/Underarm-v3.png 1500w, https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/05\/Underarm-v3-300x213.png 300w, https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/05\/Underarm-v3-1024x728.png 1024w, https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/05\/Underarm-v3-768x546.png 768w, https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/05\/Underarm-v3-18x12.png 18w, https:\/\/masterbadminton.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/05\/Underarm-v3-640x455.png 640w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 658px) 100vw, 658px\" \/><\/p>\n<p>Underarm Clears are defensive shots. They can be performed using the:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"badminton-underarm-forehand.html\"><b>Underarm Forehand Stroke<\/b><\/a><\/li>\n<li><a href=\"badminton-underarm-backhand.html\"><b>Underarm Backhand Stroke<\/b><\/a><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>Underarm Clears are hit from the forecourt. You will usually perform this shot when your opponent hits a Drop Shot to you.<\/p>\n<p><b>Here&#8217;s a flight trajectory of the Underarm Clear&#8230;<\/b><\/p>\n<div class=\"ImageBlock ImageBlockCenter\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter\" src=\"..\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/450xNxunderarm-defensive-clear-angle.jpg.pagespeed.ic.AVTKgs1ayL.jpg\" width=\"450\" data-pin-media=\"images\/underarm-defensive-clear-angle.jpg\" \/><\/div>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6px; color: #ff3300;\"><b><br \/>\nUnderarm Forehand Clear Tutorial<\/b><\/span><\/p>\n<div class=\"ImageBlock ImageBlockCenter\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter\" style=\"border: 1px solid #bab6b6;\" src=\"..\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/underarm-forehand-animation.gif\" width=\"200\" data-pin-media=\"http:\/\/www.how-to-play-badminton.com\/images\/underarm-forehand-animation.gif\" \/><\/div>\n<div class=\"CalloutBox\" style=\"box-sizing: border-box;\">\n<p>You may find it difficult to generate power for your <b>Underarm Forehand Clears<\/b>. When I was an amateur, my Underarm Forehand Clears used to land half court and my opponents used to &#8216;punish&#8217; me with a strong and steep Smash.<\/p>\n<p>In this lesson, I&#8217;ll teach you some simple tricks on how to generate power for a good Underarm Forehand Clear.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<table class=\"columns_block grid_block\" style=\"width: 100%;\" border=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"column_0\" style=\"width: 49.82%; vertical-align: top;\">\n<div class=\"ImageBlock ImageBlockCenter\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter\" src=\"..\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/250xNxbadminton-underarm-forehand-stroke-2.jpg.pagespeed.ic.XKC1l6V8rd.jpg\" width=\"250\" data-pin-media=\"images\/badminton-underarm-forehand-stroke-2.jpg\" \/><\/div>\n<\/td>\n<td class=\"column_1\" style=\"width: 50.18%; vertical-align: top;\"><b><span style=\"color: #ff3300;\">1. <\/span>Adopt the <\/b><b>Forehand Grip.<\/b> Do not grip your racket too tightly. This enables better wrist action.<\/p>\n<p><b><span style=\"color: #ff3300;\">2.<\/span> Lunge forward<\/b> <b>with your Racket Leg<\/b><b>.<\/b> Make sure you position your racket <b>in front of you<\/b>.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"column_0\" style=\"width: 49.82%; vertical-align: top;\">\n<div class=\"ImageBlock ImageBlockCenter\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter\" src=\"..\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/250xNxbadminton-underarm-forehand-stroke-wrist-relax.jpg.pagespeed.ic.5yWyNGEN8J.jpg\" width=\"250\" data-pin-media=\"images\/badminton-underarm-forehand-stroke-wrist-relax.jpg\" \/><\/div>\n<\/td>\n<td class=\"column_1\" style=\"width: 50.18%; vertical-align: top;\"><span style=\"color: #ff3300;\"><b>3.<\/b><\/span> Take the shuttle when it&#8217;s<b> in front of you<\/b>. A Common Mistake is to take it at the side of your body.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"column_0\" style=\"width: 49.82%; vertical-align: top;\">\n<div class=\"ImageBlock ImageBlockCenter\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter\" src=\"..\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/badminton-underarm-forehand-stroke-follow-through.jpg\" width=\"250\" data-pin-media=\"images\/badminton-underarm-forehand-stroke-follow-through.jpg\" \/><\/div>\n<\/td>\n<td class=\"column_1\" style=\"width: 50.18%; vertical-align: top;\"><span style=\"color: #ff3300;\"><b>4.<\/b><\/span> As you take the shuttle, <b>Bend your knees<\/b>, <b>Bend your body<\/b>, and <b>Contract your Abs<\/b>. This will help add some explosive power into your shot.<\/p>\n<p><b>Tip:<\/b> <em>Do not look at the shuttle as it flies off your racket. If you do this, your shoulder will be very stiff and you won&#8217;t be able to bend your body low for the explosive power.<\/em><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #ff3300;\"><b>5.<\/b><\/span> <b>Follow Through<\/b> with your swing for a high quality shot.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span id=\"backhand\" style=\"font-size: 18.6px; color: #ff3300;\"><b><br \/>\nUnderarm Backhand Clear Tutorial<\/b><\/span><\/p>\n<div class=\"ImageBlock ImageBlockCenter\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter\" style=\"border: 1px solid #bab6b6;\" src=\"..\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/underarm-backhand-animation.gif\" width=\"230\" data-pin-media=\"http:\/\/www.how-to-play-badminton.com\/images\/underarm-backhand-animation.gif\" \/><\/div>\n<p>The Underarm Backhand Clear is simpler than the Underarm Forehand. However, make sure you perform the right technique and play like the pros!<\/p>\n<table class=\"columns_block grid_block\" style=\"width: 100%;\" border=\"0\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"column_0\" style=\"width: 50%; vertical-align: top;\">\n<div class=\"ImageBlock ImageBlockCenter\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter\" src=\"..\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/badminton-underarm-backhand-stroke-lunge-forward.jpg\" width=\"250\" data-pin-media=\"images\/badminton-underarm-backhand-stroke-lunge-forward.jpg\" \/><\/div>\n<\/td>\n<td class=\"column_1\" style=\"width: 50%; vertical-align: top;\"><b><span style=\"color: #ff3300;\">1.<\/span> Adopt the Backhand Grip.<\/b> Don&#8217;t hold your racket too tightly.<\/p>\n<p><b><span style=\"color: #ff3300;\">2.<\/span> Lunge forward with your Racket Leg.<\/b> Make sure you position your racket <b>in front of you.<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #ff3300;\"><b>3.<\/b><\/span> Take the shuttle when it&#8217;s in front of you. Avoid taking it from the side of your body.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"column_0\" style=\"width: 50%; vertical-align: top;\">\n<div class=\"ImageBlock ImageBlockCenter\"><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"aligncenter\" src=\"..\/wp-content\/uploads\/2016\/04\/badminton-underarm-backhand-stroke-swing.jpg\" width=\"262\" data-pin-media=\"images\/badminton-underarm-backhand-stroke-swing.jpg\" \/><\/div>\n<\/td>\n<td class=\"column_1\" style=\"width: 50%; vertical-align: top;\"><span style=\"color: #ff3300;\"><b>4.<\/b><\/span> As you make contact with the shuttle, <b>Bend your knees<\/b>, <b>Bend your body<\/b>, and <b>Cont<\/b><b>ract your Abs.<\/b><\/p>\n<p><b><span style=\"color: #ff3300;\">5.<\/span> Follow Through<\/b> with your swing.<\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6px; color: #ff3300;\"><b>Underarm Backhands Are Easier Than Underarm Forehands<\/b><\/span><\/p>\n<p>Just to give you a heads up, I find the Underarm Backhand Clears easier than the Underarm Forehand Clear.<\/p>\n<p>The\u00a0Underarm Forehand has a smaller swing motion compared to the Underarm\u00a0Backhand. So it&#8217;s easier to generate power with the Underarm Backhand.<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6px; color: #ff3300;\"><b>Things to Keep in Mind<\/b><\/span><\/p>\n<p>The\u00a0Badminton Underarm Clear will usually require you to lunge forward and\u00a0hit the shuttle. As you lunge forward, you will gather some momentum.<\/p>\n<p>Some\u00a0degree of this momentum will be transferred into your underarm swinging\u00a0motion.<\/p>\n<p>You should take this into account. Control the strength of your\u00a0swing so that you don&#8217;t hit the shuttle too hard and make it fly long\u00a0the baseline!<\/p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-size: 18.6px; color: #ff3300;\"><b><br \/>\nImportant Tips and Advice<\/b><\/span><\/p>\n<ol>\n<li><b>Concentrate on Swing rather than Wrist Action.<\/b> The Badminton Underarm Clear does not require you to flick\/snap your wrist as you hit the shuttle. You only perform the quick and snapping motion of your wrist for shots such as the Overhead Backhand Clear. Focus on your swing motion; your strokes!<\/li>\n<li><b>Use your Non-Racket Arm for Balance.<\/b> I did not mention this in the tutorial above. However, you should always use your Non-Racket Arm to counterweight your Racket Arm.<\/li>\n<li><b>Not Enough Power for the Underarm Forehand Clear?\u00a0<\/b>Make sure you do these as you make contact with the shuttle; <b>Bend your body<\/b>, <b>Bend your knees<\/b>, <b>Contract your Abs<\/b> and DO NOT keep your eyes on the shuttle as it flies off your racket.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><span style=\"color: #ff3300;\"><b style=\"display: none;\">Please Like me on Facebook. Thanks!<\/b><\/span><\/p>\n<div class=\"fb-like\" data-href=\"https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/HowToPlayBadminton\" data-send=\"true\" data-width=\"100%\" data-show-faces=\"false\">\n<div id=\"COMMENTING\" class=\"fb-comment\">\n<div class=\"retnvbx\"><\/div>\n<h3><span class=\"teelmeww\">Tell me what you think!<\/span><\/h3>\n<p>What do you think about what you just read? Leave me a comment below.<\/p>\n<div class=\"fb-comments\" data-href=\"http:\/\/www.how-to-play-badminton.com\/badminton-underarm-clear.html\" data-num-posts=\"15\" data-width=\"100%\"><\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Step by step tutorial on the Badminton Underarm Clear. Learn when and how to use the defensive clear in your badminton games. <\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":0,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard",